+### Optimizer slots
+
+Optimization has three slots: **input** (command output, files and logs before they enter context), **context** (the accumulated conversation) and **output** (what the model writes). Each slot takes one optimizer, and `none` is always valid and is the baseline for every comparison.
+
+| Slot | Choices | Kind | Licence |
+|------|---------|------|---------|
+| input | `none` | built in | Apache-2.0 |
+| input | `proxy` (the `[compression.plugin]` process, headroom unless you change it) | proxy | per plugin |
+| input | `headroom` (headroom with its built-in defaults) | proxy | Apache-2.0 |
+| input | `rtk` (rewrites shell commands in the agent; only Bash tool calls) | hook | Apache-2.0 (`rtk-oss`; the full `rtk` adds BUSL-1.1 components) |
+| context | `none` | built in | Apache-2.0 |
+| output | `none` | built in | Apache-2.0 |
+
+Choose one in `.ta/daemon.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[optimizers.input]
+use = "rtk"     # none | proxy | headroom | rtk
+```
+
+Without `[optimizers.input]` the input slot follows `[compression]`: `proxy` while compression is enabled, `none` otherwise. `none` and `rtk` start no proxy and do not set `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`. Licences are recorded per optimizer and shown by `ta compression status`, which lists the selection for each slot.
+
+Every reduction an optimizer makes keeps the full original on disk (content-addressed under `.ta/optimizer-originals/`), and its metrics record carries `original_ref`, so any reduction can be inspected or undone.
+
+Compare optimizers on a captured goal with a golden replay, without editing config:
+
+```bash
+ta golden replay <id> --set optimizers.input.use=none --tag no-optimizer
+ta golden replay <id> --set optimizers.input.use=rtk --tag rtk
+ta golden report
+```
+
+An unknown name fails before any checkout or goal is created and lists the valid choices.
+
+### No visible windows, and the flap guard
+
+On Windows every optimizer process is started with `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, so a console child never opens a window. If an optimizer fails five times in five minutes, TA disables it with one message, runs agents without it, and does not restart it again until you do:
+
+```bash
+ta compression status   # restart count and last failure
+ta compression enable   # resume after fixing the cause
+```
+
